   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Independent voltage sources become short circuits, while independent current sources become open circuits.",
    "imageQuery": "electrical wiring schematic",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "Vind = 0 (SC), Iind = 0 (OC)",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Dependent sources cannot be deactivated because their controlling variables depend on network conditions.",
    "imageQuery": "circuit breadboard close up",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "icon",
     "caption": "",
     "items": [
      {
       "label": "Dependent Source",
       "symbol": "💠"
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Their values change dynamically based on voltages or currents elsewhere in the circuit.",
    "imageQuery": "oscilloscope screen testing",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "Vdep = f(Vx, Ix)",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Instead, we deactivate independent sources and apply a test voltage or test current at the terminals.",
    "imageQuery": "electronic test equipment multimeter",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "compare",
     "caption": "",
     "items": [
      {
       "label": "Vtest applied",
       "symbol": "🔋"
      },
      {
       "label": "Find Itest",
       "symbol": "📈"
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "If we apply a test voltage V test, we determine the resulting injected current I test.",
    "imageQuery": "electrical multimeter measuring",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "sketch",
     "sketch": "flowchart",
     "caption": "",
     "params": {
      "labelA": "Test Method"
     },
     "items": []
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "The Thevenin resistance then equals the ratio of test voltage to test current.",
    "imageQuery": "electronic bench testing",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "Rth = Vtest / Itest",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Alternatively, you can divide open circuit voltage by short circuit current across the terminals.",
    "imageQuery": "technician checking circuitry",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "Rth = Voc / Isc",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
   {
